From: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: bound and serialize RX-lock recovery

Port the RX diagnostic and recovery changes onto the current PCS stack,
keeping the SDK crossing-search calibration, TX FIR override and current
PHY bringup sequence. Retain the existing USXGMII speed replay and reject
unsupported XFI speeds instead of programming uninitialized values.

Report register failures and local receiver loss as link down. Serialize
CDR recovery with both configuration callbacks and explicit AN restarts,
and track the selected interface per port. Allow two recovery resets one
second apart, then hold a 30-second cooldown. Observe for one second again
after expiry; partial receiver lock must not discard the cooldown. Require
one second of signal loss before starting a new recovery epoch.

Leave pause configuration to pcs_config instead of unconditionally
enabling it in post_config. This keeps the pause policy independent of
callback ordering; the current phylink calls post_config first.

Signed-off-by: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
